// A widened primitive is a BORROW, exactly like a widened class: the fat pointer points at a compound
// literal with the enclosing block's storage duration. Returning it would hand back a pointer into a dead
// frame, so the escape check that already governs contract values governs this too — the new capability
// needed no new safety machinery, and this fixture is what says so.
fn Hashable leak() {
    int32 n = 1;
    Hashable h = n;
    return h;
}

fn int32 main() { return 0; }
